 vary regional cluster area smoothly. A cluster can represent many people; never render one particle per person. Use a bounded fixed particle pool and projected land anchors. Any births, deaths or movement depicted without a demographic flows dataset must be identified as symbolic.","change":"Changes between stock totals are net population change, combining births, deaths, migration and possible source/model revisions. Net increase is not a birth count; net decrease is not a death count. Never derive mortality rates, per-capita atrocity comparisons or afterlife destinations from these values.","uncertainty":"Ancient values are reconstructions with substantial uncertainty and do not establish within-continent settlement patterns. Source changes at 1800 and 1950 may introduce breaks. Values for 2024–2026 are projections, even when shown on a present-day timeline.","worldTotals":"World is retained independently from the source, not recomputed from the continent totals; small differences may exist due to grouping, rounding or source treatment.","attribution":"Keep the dataset citation and source links in the page evidence panel. OWID processing is CC BY 4.0; original providers retain their applicable terms."},"sources":[{"title":"OWID population series and processing notes","url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/population-regions-with-projections","role":"Distributor, aggregation and source-transition methodology"},{"title":"HYDE v3.3 dataset DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.24416/UU01-AEZZIT","role":"Original historical dataset linked from OWID; DOI target not readable by current web tool"},{"title":"Klein Goldewijk et al. (2017), Anthropogenic land use estimates for the Holocene — HYDE 3.2","url":"https://essd.copernicus.org/articles/9/927/2017/","role":"Primary methods paper for predecessor model, not the 3.3 numbers"},{"title":"Gapminder population documentation","url":"https://www.gapminder.org/data/documentation/gd003/","role":"Original population compilation us